## Hints

- E1: all three routes to α̂ are the same identity rearranged; part
  (c) is: mean(y) − mean(ŷ − α̂)... simpler: mean(y) − β̂·mean(x) IS
  (b). The point is to see α̂ = ȳ − β̂x̄ from three sides.
- E2: use np.allclose with atol=1e-10; the no-intercept refit breaks
  (i) visibly if mean(x) ≠ 0, since x'e = −n·intercept·mean... derive
  it: without intercept, x'e = 0 still holds (first-order condition!)
  but Σe ≠ 0 in general.
- E3: corr(r_dm, r_SPY) ≈ 0 exactly in-sample because corr(e, x) = 0
  and α̂ is a constant.
- E4: identity (ii) — e is orthogonal to x — so big-|e| days are
  cross-sectionally NOT big-|x| days on average... but check: are
  they? A scatter of e vs x will show you the variance fan first.
